gine/godot/pull/123123#issuecomment-5532022657","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123123","id":5532022657,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSbv3gQ","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-03T20:56:02Z","updated_at":"2026-09-03T20:56:02Z","body":"> Though this is weird, I saw some CI issues in between rebases, got curious, and after looking around a bit, I found that some code from upstream, i.e.:\r\n> \r\n> https://github.com/KhronosGroup/OpenXR-SDK-Source/blob/2b99fec95e9cdf352c1a98e9cb23bf4def1cf8e6/src/loader/runtime_interface.cpp#L298-L317\r\n> \r\n> doesn't seem to be a part of this PR. Something like this shouldn't happen without adding a patch and giving reasoning behind the decision, unless it's something trivial.\r\n\r\nYes, I add to update `runtime_interface.cpp` and `api_layer_interface.cpp` to remove the `try...catch`, they were causing CI to fail since exception is disabled for the project.\r\n\r\nI consider the removal trivial, but can add a patch if you think it's necessary.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.git